{#
  Grid charging plan for the two house batteries (Tibber 15-min prices + PV forecast). Used by sensor.netzladeplan
  (integrations/energie_automatik.yaml), recalculated every 15 minutes. Returns JSON.

  ladeplan(): rolling decision for the current 15-min slot - charge from the grid, hold the batteries, or normal
    - horizon: until the end of the known Tibber prices (from ~13:00 tomorrow 24:00), at least until the next 11:00;
      before tomorrow's prices are published until tomorrow 11:00 (those slots use the price 24 h earlier), so that
      energy left at midnight still counts for the night and the morning
    - per 15-min slot: consumption = hausverbrauch_w() (14-day average without the cars), PV as a sine over the
      unshaded window sunrise + 2 h .. sunset - 2.5 h (user's observation: shade from ~16:00 in October, before 14:00
      at the winter solstice); today = pv_rest_heute() spread over the rest of today's window, tomorrow = forecast
      tomorrow x pv_faktor_plan() (cautious: the worse half of the last 14 days, capped like today), today too
      until the real PV can confirm it; net = consumption - PV
    - today's PV is capped twice (06.11.2026: the model said 6-11 kW, real 1.5-1.9 kW, the charge came 1.75 h late):
      the whole-day sine never exceeds today's yield + the remaining forecast (squeezing the remaining forecast into
      the end of the window blew it up), and the PV now never exceeds 1.3 x the real PV (sensor.pv_leistung_20_minuten,
      20-min average) + 0.3 kW - the rest of the day is scaled down with it
    - surplus block = the PV surplus slots (net < -0.1 kWh) of the first sunny day in the horizon, S = its net surplus.
      Before the block only the stored energy serves the house; after it the stored energy AND S. If S fills the
      batteries anyway, only the slots before the block count (the old rule "bridge until the PV takes over"). If not
      (autumn/winter), the slots after the block count too, up to the next surplus block or the horizon end - the
      evening peak must not be forgotten (09.11.2026: 8.9 kWh would have gone at 0.56-0.65 EUR in the morning, the
      evening cost 0.88-0.96 EUR)
    - The stored energy (usable 2 x 16 kWh x 90 %, above the backup reserves -> 27.4 kWh) should serve the MOST EXPENSIVE slots, not simply
      the next ones (in normal mode the inverters discharge at once). S only serves slots after the block.
    - laden: the uncovered slots before t* (next slot >= 1 ct cheaper) that cost >= price now / 0.9 (losses)
      + input_number.mindestvorteil_netzladen need >= 0.5 kWh -> charge that energy now (target SoC + 3 %, 5 % steps;
      max price input_number.max_ladepreis_netz). Energy for slots after the block only as far as S still fits.
    - halten: the battery energy is reserved for later slots that are >= 2 ct more expensive than now -> hold the
      batteries until the first of them ("bis"). Never while the model sees PV surplus now (the PV must go into the
      batteries; the real surplus is handled by 'Preis-Automatik: PV-Ueberschuss trotz Halten in den Akku').
    - otherwise kein Bedarf / warten (cheaper slot ahead) / kein Vorteil, season off -> Sommer
  Forecast.Solar ignores the shading (buildings, mountains): pv_rest_heute() multiplies the
  forecast with sensor.pv_prognose_faktor and caps it at 1.1 x the best real day of the season (pv_historie.jinja).
  soc_test / pv_rest_test / verbrauch_test (kWh per day) / jetzt_test (ISO time) / pv_ist_test (kW) / ertrag_test
  (kWh today) only override the inputs for testing.

  pv_rest_heute(): usable PV for the rest of today (kWh) - remaining forecast x factor, never more than the
  seasonal cap minus today's yield. Also used by the battery protection while a car charges.
  pv_roh(): the raw forecast and yield values, corrected for the minutes after midnight before they refresh.
#}

{% macro _eur(v) %}{{ ('%.3f' | format(v)) | replace('.', ',') }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro _kwh(v) %}{{ (v | round(1) | string) | replace('.', ',') }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro _uhr(t, heute) %}{{ t.strftime('%H:%M') }}{{ ' (morgen)' if t.date() > heute else '' }}{% endmacro %}

{% macro hausverbrauch_w() -%}
{#- planning load in W plus its source, "W|source": 14-day average without the cars (statistics helper on
    sensor.hausverbrauch_ohne_autos); while that still builds up (< ~3 days of data) the old 3-day average,
    else input_number.hausverbrauch_pro_tag. The load varies a lot (washing on cheap days, PCs, split AC),
    so only a long average is useful (user 24.10.2026). -#}
{%- set neu = states('sensor.hausverbrauch_ohne_autos_14_tage') | float(-1) -%}
{%- set alt = states('sensor.hausverbrauch_3_tage') | float(-1) -%}
{%- if neu > 0 and state_attr('sensor.hausverbrauch_ohne_autos_14_tage', 'age_coverage_ratio') | float(0) >= 0.2 -%}
{{- neu | round(0) | int }}|Ø 14 Tage ohne Autos
{%- elif alt > 0 -%}
{{- alt | round(0) | int }}|Ø 3 Tage
{%- else -%}
{{- (states('input_number.hausverbrauch_pro_tag') | float(17) * 1000 / 24) | round(0) | int }}|fester Wert
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro ladeplan(soc_test=none, pv_rest_test=none, verbrauch_test=none, jetzt_test=none, pv_ist_test=none, ertrag_test=none) -%}
{%- set eta = 0.9 -%}
{%- set tol = 0.01 -%}
{%- set tol_h = 0.02 -%}
{%- set jetzt = now() if jetzt_test is none else as_local(as_datetime(jetzt_test)) -%}
{%- set slot0 = jetzt.replace(minute=(jetzt.minute // 15) * 15, second=0, microsecond=0) -%}
{%- set elf = jetzt.replace(hour=11, minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0) -%}
{%- set ende11 = elf if jetzt.hour < 11 else elf + timedelta(days=1) -%}
{%- set allp = state_attr('sensor.tibber_preise', 'prices') or [] -%}
{%- set pend = (as_datetime(allp[-1].s) + timedelta(minutes=15)) if allp | count > 0 else ende11 -%}
{%- set ende = ende11 if ende11 > pend else pend -%}
{%- set morgen = (jetzt + timedelta(days=1)).date() -%}
{#- tomorrow's prices not published yet: plan on until tomorrow 11:00 with the prices 24 h earlier, so that energy
    left at midnight still counts for the night and the morning (only while that day's PV is modelled) -#}
{%- if ende == pend and as_local(pend).hour == 0 and as_local(pend).date() <= morgen -%}
  {%- set ende = as_local(pend) + timedelta(hours=11) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set hv = hausverbrauch_w().split('|') -%}
{%- set last_kw = hv[0] | float(700) / 1000 -%}
{%- set quelle = hv[1] if hv | count > 1 else '?' -%}
{%- if verbrauch_test is not none -%}{%- set last_kw = verbrauch_test / 24 -%}{%- set quelle = 'Test' -%}{%- endif -%}
{#- battery_level of the Sungrows is relative to their min..max SoC window (0 % = min SoC, it moves in steps of
    1.11 % = 1 % cell SoC; WR2 showed 0.0 % at its 10 % min SoC on 10.11.2026), usable 16 kWh x 90 % = 14.4 kWh per
    inverter. Normal mode stops at the backup reserve (WR1 10 %, WR2 0 %, same scale). Until 10.11.2026 the plan
    took the 10 % min SoC off a second time (at 25 % it saw 5.0 instead of 5.9 kWh). -#}
{%- set k1 = states('sensor.battery_capacity') | float(16) * (states('sensor.max_soc') | float(100) - states('sensor.min_soc') | float(10)) / 100 -%}
{%- set k2 = states('sensor.wr2_battery_capacity') | float(16) * (states('sensor.wr2_max_soc') | float(100) - states('sensor.wr2_min_soc') | float(10)) / 100 -%}
{%- set r1 = states('sensor.reserved_soc_for_backup') | float(0) -%}
{%- set r2 = states('sensor.wr2_reserved_soc_for_backup') | float(0) -%}
{%- set l1 = states('sensor.battery_level') | float(0) if soc_test is none else soc_test -%}
{%- set l2 = states('sensor.wr2_battery_level') | float(0) if soc_test is none else soc_test -%}
{%- set soc = (l1 + l2) / 2 -%}
{%- set kap = (k1 * (100 - r1) + k2 * (100 - r2)) / 100 -%}
{%- set e0 = (k1 * ([l1 - r1, 0] | max) + k2 * ([l2 - r2, 0] | max)) / 100 -%}
{%- set pv_rest = pv_rest_heute() | float(0) -%}
{%- if pv_rest_test is not none -%}{%- set pv_rest = pv_rest_test -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set f_norm = states('sensor.pv_prognose_faktor') | float(1) -%}
{%- set f_plan = pv_faktor_plan() | float(f_norm) -%}
{%- set pv_ist = (states('sensor.pv_leistung_20_minuten') | float(-1000) / 1000) if pv_ist_test is none else pv_ist_test -%}
{%- set unter = as_datetime(state_attr('sun.sun', 'next_setting')) -%}
{%- set auf = as_datetime(state_attr('sun.sun', 'next_rising')) -%}
{%- if auf > unter -%}{%- set auf = auf - timedelta(days=1) -%}{%- endif -%}
{#- unshaded PV window of that day; other days are shifted by whole days (a few minutes off, good enough) -#}
{%- set a0 = auf + timedelta(hours=2) -%}
{%- set L = [(unter - timedelta(hours=2, minutes=30) - a0).total_seconds(), 3600] | max -%}
{%- set d0 = as_local(a0).date() -%}
{#- today's remaining PV goes into the rest of today's window: scale it to a whole-day sine -#}
{%- set xj = (jetzt - a0 - timedelta(days=(jetzt.date() - d0).days)).total_seconds() / L -%}
{#- until the real PV can tell (first 10 % of today's window, or no PV reading) today counts with the cautious
    factor like tomorrow; after that the normal factor, cut down by cap 2 if the real PV stays below it -#}
{%- set vorsicht = (xj <= 0.1 or pv_ist < 0) and pv_rest_test is none and f_norm > 0 -%}
{%- if vorsicht -%}{%- set pv_rest = pv_rest * f_plan / f_norm -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set anteil = 1 if xj <= 0 else (0 if xj >= 1 else (1 + cos(pi * xj)) / 2) -%}
{%- set pv_tag = (pv_rest / ([anteil, 0.05] | max)) if anteil > 0 else 0 -%}
{#- cap 1: the whole-day sine never exceeds today's yield + the remaining forecast -#}
{%- set roh = pv_roh() | from_json -%}
{%- set ertrag = roh.ertrag if ertrag_test is none else ertrag_test -%}
{%- set pv_tag = [pv_tag, ertrag + pv_rest] | min -%}
{#- cap 2: PV now <= 1.3 x real PV (20-min average) + 0.3 kW, the rest of today scaled down with it -#}
{%- set p_mod = (pv_tag * pi / 2 * sin(pi * xj) / (L / 3600)) if 0 < xj < 1 else 0 -%}
{%- set kappung = ((1.3 * pv_ist + 0.3) / p_mod) if (0.1 < xj < 0.9 and pv_ist >= 0 and p_mod > 1.3 * pv_ist + 0.3) else 1 -%}
{%- set pv_tag = pv_tag * kappung -%}
{%- from 'pv_historie.jinja' import pv_hist -%}
{%- set hist_m = pv_hist(jetzt + timedelta(days=1)) | from_json -%}
{%- set pv_morgen = roh.morgen * f_plan -%}
{%- if hist_m.max is defined -%}{%- set pv_morgen = [pv_morgen, hist_m.max * 1.1] | min -%}{%- endif -%}
{#- index of the current slot in the price list -#}
{%- set ns = namespace(j0=-1) -%}
{%- for x in allp -%}{%- if ns.j0 < 0 and as_datetime(x.s) > slot0 - timedelta(minutes=15) -%}{%- set ns.j0 = loop.index0 -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{#- slots now .. horizon end: price, PV energy (kWh per slot), date -#}
{%- set n = ((ende - slot0).total_seconds() // 900) | int -%}
{%- set s = namespace(p=[], pv=[], d=[], ok=true) -%}
{%- for i in range(n) if s.ok and ns.j0 >= 0 -%}
  {%- set j = ns.j0 + i -%}
  {%- if j < allp | count -%}{%- set p = allp[j].p -%}
  {%- elif j - 96 >= 0 and j - 96 < allp | count -%}{%- set p = allp[j - 96].p -%}
  {%- else -%}{%- set p = none -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if p is none -%}{%- set s.ok = false -%}{%- else -%}
    {%- set tm = slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * i + 7.5) -%}
    {%- set td = as_local(tm).date() -%}
    {%- set x = (tm - a0 - timedelta(days=(td - d0).days)).total_seconds() / L -%}
    {%- set e_tag = pv_tag if td == jetzt.date() else (pv_morgen if td == morgen else 0) -%}
    {%- set pv = (e_tag * pi / 2 * sin(pi * x) * 900 / L) if 0 < x < 1 else 0 -%}
    {%- set s.p = s.p + [p] -%}{%- set s.pv = s.pv + [pv] -%}{%- set s.d = s.d + [td] -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set m = s.p | count -%}
{%- set p0 = s.p[0] if m > 0 else none -%}
{%- set max_preis = states('input_number.max_ladepreis_netz') | float(0.25) -%}
{%- set vorteil = states('input_number.mindestvorteil_netzladen') | float(0.03) -%}
{#- net load per slot; surplus block [b0, b1) = PV surplus slots of the first sunny day, r2 = start of the next
    block (cuts the horizon) -#}
{%- set c = namespace(net=[], b0=m, b1=m, r2=m, ts=m, bi=-1, bp=999) -%}
{%- for i in range(m) -%}{%- set c.net = c.net + [last_kw * 0.25 - s.pv[i]] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{#- the current slot uses the real PV (20-min average) instead of the model: the 1.3 x + 0.3 kW tolerance of cap 2
    must not hide that the house draws from the battery right now -#}
{%- if m > 0 and pv_ist >= 0 -%}{%- set c.net = [(last_kw - pv_ist) * 0.25] + c.net[1:] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- for i in range(m) if c.b0 == m and c.net[i] < -0.1 -%}{%- set c.b0 = i -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- for i in range(c.b0, m) if c.net[i] < -0.1 and s.d[i] == s.d[c.b0] -%}{%- set c.b1 = i + 1 -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- for i in range(c.b1, m) if c.r2 == m and c.net[i] < -0.1 -%}{%- set c.r2 = i -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- for i in range(c.r2) -%}
  {%- if i >= 1 and c.ts == m and s.p[i] <= s.p[0] - tol -%}{%- set c.ts = i -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.p[i] < c.bp -%}{%- set c.bp = s.p[i] -%}{%- set c.bi = i -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set c.ts = [c.ts, c.r2] | min -%}
{#- S = net PV surplus of the block, dvor = what the house needs before it; voll = the PV fills the batteries even
    if they serve everything before the block -#}
{%- set e = namespace(s=0, dvor=0) -%}
{%- for i in range(c.b0, c.b1) -%}{%- set e.s = e.s - c.net[i] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- for i in range(c.b0) if c.net[i] > 0 -%}{%- set e.dvor = e.dvor + c.net[i] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- set S = [e.s, 0] | max -%}
{%- set voll = c.b0 < m and S >= kap - ([e0 - e.dvor, 0] | max) - 0.5 -%}
{%- set mit_nach = c.b0 < m and not voll and c.b1 < c.r2 -%}
{%- set hz = c.r2 if mit_nach else c.b0 -%}
{#- slots that need energy: before the block, and after it if the PV does not fill the batteries -#}
{%- set k = namespace(l=[]) -%}
{%- for i in range(c.b0) if c.net[i] > 0.01 -%}{%- set k.l = k.l + [{'i': i, 'p': s.p[i], 'd': c.net[i], 'n': false}] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- if mit_nach -%}
  {%- for i in range(c.b1, c.r2) if c.net[i] > 0.01 -%}{%- set k.l = k.l + [{'i': i, 'p': s.p[i], 'd': c.net[i], 'n': true}] -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{#- The battery energy (ra) serves the most expensive slots, S (rb) only slots after the block - first, it cannot
    serve anything else. Charging now pays for the uncovered slots before t* whose price >= price now / 0.9 +
    minimum advantage. -#}
{%- set kosten = (p0 / eta + vorteil) if p0 is not none else 99 -%}
{%- set g = namespace(ra=e0, rb=(S if mit_nach else 0), cut=-1, alle=true, qv=0, qn=0, qw=0, avor=0) -%}
{%- for x in k.l | sort(attribute='p', reverse=true) -%}
  {%- set covb = ([g.rb, x.d] | min) if x.n else 0 -%}
  {%- set g.rb = g.rb - covb -%}
  {%- set d = x.d - covb -%}
  {%- set cova = [g.ra, d] | min -%}
  {%- if g.ra > 0.001 and d > 0.001 -%}{%- set g.cut = x.p -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set g.ra = g.ra - cova -%}
  {%- if not x.n -%}{%- set g.avor = g.avor + cova -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- set offen = d - cova -%}
  {%- if offen > 0.001 -%}{%- set g.alle = false -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if 1 <= x.i < c.ts and x.p >= kosten and offen > 0.001 -%}
    {%- if x.n -%}{%- set g.qn = g.qn + offen -%}{%- else -%}{%- set g.qv = g.qv + offen -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- set g.qw = g.qw + offen * x.p -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{#- energy for slots after the block has to sit in the batteries next to S -#}
{%- set raum_nach = kap - (S if mit_nach else 0) - (e0 - g.avor) -%}
{%- set q = g.qv + ([g.qn, [raum_nach, 0] | max] | min) -%}
{%- set bedarf = [q, kap - e0] | min -%}
{%- set soll = e0 + bedarf -%}
{#- level (both inverters) that holds soll: both above their backup reserve, else only the one with the lower reserve -#}
{%- set lv = (soll * 100 + k1 * r1 + k2 * r2) / (k1 + k2) -%}
{%- if lv < [r1, r2] | max -%}{%- set lv = ([r1, r2] | min) + soll * 100 / (k2 if r2 <= r1 else k1) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set ziel_soc = [[((lv + 3) / 5) | round(0, 'ceil') * 5, soc | round(0, 'ceil')] | max, 100] | min | int -%}
{#- hold: battery energy is reserved for later, more expensive slots and the house would use it now -#}
{%- set cut = -1 if g.alle else g.cut -%}
{%- set h = namespace(bis=none, nach=99) -%}
{%- for i in range(1, c.r2) if h.bis is none and s.p[i] >= cut - tol_h -%}{%- set h.bis = i -%}{%- endfor -%}
{#- no hold if the batteries can be refilled from the grid before the expensive slots for less than the price now
    (price there / 0.9 + minimum advantage, not above the max. charge price) by at least 2 ct: then use them now and
    charge later. The 2 ct keep the hold from flapping every 15 min around that threshold (09.11. 21:45-22:15) -#}
{%- for i in range(1, h.bis if h.bis is not none else c.r2) if s.p[i] <= max_preis -%}
  {%- set h.nach = [h.nach, s.p[i] / eta + vorteil] | min -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set halten = cut > 0 and e0 >= 0.5 and m > 0 and c.net[0] > 0 and p0 < cut - tol_h and p0 < h.nach + tol_h -%}
{%- set bis = slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * (h.bis if (halten and h.bis is not none) else c.ts)) -%}
{%- set vergleich = (g.qw / (g.qv + g.qn)) if (g.qv + g.qn) > 0.05 else (cut if halten else none) -%}
{%- set t_hz = slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * hz) -%}
{%- set t_ende = slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * m) -%}
{%- if not is_state('binary_sensor.netzladen_saison', 'on') -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'Sommer' -%}{%- set grund = 'Sommer-Saison: nur PV' -%}
{%- elif m == 0 -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'keine Preise' -%}{%- set grund = 'Keine Tibber-Preise vorhanden' -%}
{%- elif bedarf >= 0.5 and p0 > max_preis -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'zu teuer' -%}{%- set grund = 'Preis jetzt ' ~ _eur(p0) ~ ' € über Max. ' ~ _eur(max_preis) ~ ' €' -%}
{%- elif bedarf >= 0.5 -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'laden' -%}
  {%- set grund = 'Jetzt laden bis ' ~ ziel_soc ~ ' % (' ~ _eur(p0) ~ ' € statt Ø ' ~ _eur(vergleich) ~ ' € in den teuren Viertelstunden, ' ~ _kwh(bedarf) ~ ' kWh)' -%}
{%- elif halten -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'halten' -%}
  {%- set grund = 'Akku halten bis ' ~ _uhr(bis, jetzt.date()) ~ ': ' ~ _kwh(e0) ~ ' kWh für die Spitze ab ' ~ _eur(cut) ~ ' € aufheben (jetzt ' ~ _eur(p0) ~ ' €)' -%}
{%- elif g.alle and voll -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'kein Bedarf' -%}
  {%- set grund = 'Akku (' ~ _kwh(e0) ~ ' kWh) reicht bis ' ~ _uhr(t_hz, jetzt.date()) ~ ', dann füllt die PV ihn' -%}
{%- elif g.alle -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'kein Bedarf' -%}
  {%- set grund = 'Akku (' ~ _kwh(e0) ~ ' kWh)' ~ ((' und PV (' ~ _kwh(S) ~ ' kWh)') if mit_nach else '') ~ ' reichen bis ' ~ _uhr(slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * c.r2), jetzt.date()) -%}
{%- elif c.ts < c.r2 -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'warten' -%}
  {%- set grund = 'Günstiger laden ab ' ~ _uhr(slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * c.ts), jetzt.date()) ~ ' (' ~ _eur(s.p[c.ts]) ~ ' €)' -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- set zustand = 'kein Vorteil' -%}
  {%- set grund = 'Jetzt ' ~ _eur(p0) ~ ' € (+ Verluste) lohnt für keine teurere Viertelstunde bis ' ~ _uhr(slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * c.r2), jetzt.date()) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{{- {
  'zustand': zustand, 'laden': zustand == 'laden', 'halten': zustand == 'halten', 'grund': grund, 'ziel_soc': ziel_soc,
  'preis_jetzt': p0, 'vergleichspreis': (vergleich | round(4)) if vergleich is not none else none,
  'spitze_ab': (cut | round(4)) if cut > 0 else none,
  'bedarf_kwh': bedarf | round(1), 'soll_kwh': soll | round(1), 'akku_kwh': e0 | round(1), 'pv_rest_kwh': pv_rest | round(1),
  'pv_ueberschuss_kwh': S | round(1), 'pv_fuellt_akku': voll, 'pv_kappung': kappung | round(2),
  'pv_faktor_plan': f_plan, 'pv_vorsichtig': vorsicht,
  'pv_jetzt_kw': (pv_ist | round(2)) if pv_ist >= 0 else none,
  'verbrauch_w': (last_kw * 1000) | round(0) | int, 'verbrauch_quelle': quelle,
  'bis': bis.isoformat(), 'horizont_ende': (slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * c.r2)).isoformat(),
  'pv_ab': (slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * c.b0)).isoformat() if c.b0 < m else none,
  'pv_bis': (slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * c.b1)).isoformat() if c.b0 < m else none,
  'guenstigste_zeit': (slot0 + timedelta(minutes=15 * c.bi)).isoformat() if c.bi >= 0 else none,
  'guenstigster_preis': c.bp if c.bi >= 0 else none
} | tojson -}}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro pv_rest_heute() -%}
{%- from 'pv_historie.jinja' import pv_hist -%}
{%- set hist = pv_hist(now()) | from_json -%}
{%- set roh = pv_roh() | from_json -%}
{%- set rest = roh.rest * states('sensor.pv_prognose_faktor') | float(1) -%}
{%- if hist.max is defined -%}
  {%- set rest = [rest, hist.max * 1.1 - roh.ertrag] | min -%}
{%- endif -%}
{{- ([rest, 0] | max) | round(1) -}}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro pv_roh(heute=none) -%}
{#- raw Forecast.Solar values (remaining today, tomorrow) and today's yield, JSON. Around midnight they lag: Forecast.Solar
    refreshes hourly at :17, so from 00:00 until then "today" still holds yesterday (remaining 0) and "tomorrow"
    holds today; the inverters reset their daily yield at ~00:04 (10.11.2026: at 00:00 the plan saw no PV for today,
    surplus 1.2 instead of 6.3 kWh). A forecast last reported before today: its "tomorrow" is today (and stands in for
    tomorrow too, until the refresh); a yield last changed before today counts 0. heute only for testing. -#}
{%- set d = now().date() if heute is none else heute -%}
{%- set fc = states.sensor.energy_production_today -%}
{%- set alt = fc is not none and as_local(fc.last_reported).date() < d -%}
{%- set morgen = states('sensor.energy_production_tomorrow') | float(0) -%}
{%- set rest = morgen if alt else states('sensor.energy_production_today_remaining') | float(0) -%}
{%- set y = states.sensor.sum_daily_pv_generation -%}
{%- set ertrag = 0 if (y is none or as_local(y.last_changed).date() < d) else states('sensor.sum_daily_pv_generation') | float(0) -%}
{{- {'rest': rest, 'morgen': morgen, 'ertrag': ertrag, 'alt': alt} | tojson -}}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro pv_faktor_plan() -%}
{#- cautious PV factor for the days the real PV cannot confirm yet: mean of the worse half of the daily quotes
    real / forecast of the last 14 days (sensor.pv_prognose_faktor, attribute tage), 0.2 .. the normal factor.
    In November the quotes split into fog days (0.13-0.26) and 0.6-1.0, and the shading grows
    towards the solstice; the 14-day average (0.70) planned 6-10 kWh PV on fog days (09./10.11.2026: 2.0 / 3.5 kWh
    real). Missing PV costs the evening peak (~0.25 EUR/kWh more), PV on top only shifts a night charge. -#}
{%- set f = states('sensor.pv_prognose_faktor') | float(1) -%}
{%- set q = namespace(l=[]) -%}
{%- for t in state_attr('sensor.pv_prognose_faktor', 'tage') or [] if t.prog | float(0) > 1 -%}
  {%- set q.l = q.l + [t.ist | float(0) / t.prog | float(1)] -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set n = (q.l | count + 1) // 2 -%}
{%- set fp = ((q.l | sort)[:n] | sum / n) if n > 0 else f -%}
{{- ([[fp, 0.2] | max, f] | min) | round(2) -}}
{%- endmacro %}
